{"dog":{"age_group":"adult","application_url":"https://petstablished.com/public/search/redirect?application_type=adoption&pet_id=2876671&premium=true","availability_detail":"available","breed_display":"Medium mixed breed","breed_primary":"Mixed Breed","description_text":"Meet Lola, the sweetest girl waiting for her happy ending! ❤️\n\nLola's story begins with a heartbreaking note. She was left outside a cat rescue in Brooklyn, wearing a sweatshirt that read, \"My name is Lola, please help me.\" We don't know much about what her life looked like before that night, but we do know that whoever welcomes this incredibly sweet girl into their home will be very lucky.\n\nLola is estimated to be between 3 and 5 years old and weighs 63 pounds. Despite everything she's been through, she's one of the sweetest dogs you could hope to meet. She's still settling into foster care, and we're getting to know her personality a little more each day, but so far, she's been an absolute pleasure to have around.\n\nAnd this girl has some seriously impressive house manners! Lola is house-trained, does beautifully in her crate, and can be left home alone for a full day without issue.\n\nLola is a quiet soul who’s happiest curled up next to her people. The second you sit down, she’s ready to hop up beside you, and if you stop petting her too soon, she’ll give you a gentle paw for more. About the only thing that gets her off the couch that quickly is hearing, “Do you want to go for a walk?” She perks right up, ready for a leisurely stroll around town with her exceptional leash skills. She’s also treat-motivated and fun to train, especially when there’s a snack in it for her.\n\nLola's next chapter deserves to be so much better than her last. We're hoping to find her a loving home where she'll feel safe, cherished, and never have to wonder where she belongs again.","detail_url":"https://petstablished.com/public/search/pet/2876671","id":"cff48b6d05ab53ef6b27b6ce361696a0","image_urls":["https://s